          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "间 — jiān — \"measure word for rooms\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "后边有两间书房 hòubian yǒu liǎng jiān shūfáng — There are two studies at the back."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 间 (jiān) — seven strokes: the door piece 门, three strokes, and 日 inside it, four strokes. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "间 (jiān) is inherited from Middle Chinese kean (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which writes it another way and glosses it 'a gap' and 'in between': the space between walls, and so a room."
            }
          ]
        },
